{
  "slug": "cpln",
  "name": "Cpln",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Deploy and manage workloads on Control Plane — the AI-native virtual cloud spanning AWS, GCP, Azure, OCI, and bare metal under one API. Ships 23 skills, 8 guided agents, production guardrails, and a hosted MCP server so your assistant runs cpln correctly, grants credential-free cloud access via Universal Cloud Identity, sets up domains and secrets, and migrates off Kubernetes without hallucinating commands or eyeballing manifests.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **30 skills**, **2 agents**, **2 commands**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (30): `access-control` (Primary skill for access control, policies, and RBAC on Control Plane), `audit-compliance` (Audit trail and compliance on Control Plane), `autoscaling-capacity` (Workload autoscaling and Capacity AI on Control Plane), `cdn-rate-limiting` (CDN caching and request rate limiting for Control Plane workloads), `cpln` (Writes cpln CLI commands and workflows for Control Plane), `domain` (Custom domains for Control Plane workloads), `environment-promotion` (Promotes workloads across dev/staging/production on Control Plane), `external-logging` (Ships Control Plane org logs to external providers), and 22 more\n- **Agents** (2): `k8s-migrator` (Use when migrating from Kubernetes, Docker Compose, or Helm to Control Plane), `workload-troubleshooter` (Use when a Control Plane workload is unhealthy, crashing, not starting, or behaving unexpectedly)\n- **Commands** (2): `migrate-k8s` (Migrate Kubernetes manifests, Docker Compose projects, or Helm charts to Control Plane), `troubleshoot` (Diagnose and fix a Control Plane workload that is unhealthy or not working correctly)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `cpln`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install cpln@claude-community` from `controlplane-com/ai-plugin` (`plugins/cpln`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
